 "note": "The Gargoyle f02-f74 (gargoyle.py), WIP: 22/73 pass (IoU 0.861, dE 16.1) after re-measuring f30 (broad trapezoid wings, leaf ears to +-22 px, a body filling the chest), the fixed placement scale (k 0.37 -> 0.25), place_frames 21-33, egg/crouch/wrap priors, look + optimfail with spread x wrap and crouch probes. Most failures are dE 16.2-18.5 at IoU 0.86-0.88 (the rising crouch f02-f19, the fold f33-f49, the egg frames); a root-to-tip wing ramp did not help (the look chose it flat). Round 10: the render is too FLAT (f10 brightness p10/p50/p90 44/85/108 vs the source 24/99/181), but the contrast is pose-dependent (f50 source median 66 vs f10 99) while ours stays ~100: a strong key (5) + low ambient widened the range yet raised the mean dE 16.1 -> 17.1 -> reverted. Needs curved wing membranes whose shading changes with the wing pose. The sheet is TWO animations: f02-f41 (median brightness 41-132, bright stone) and f42-f74, where a RED ball (41,0,0 .. 255,0,0; 36-146 px) rises from the body (rows 25-36 at f42) to above the head (rows 0-12 from f50) and the stone renders darker (median 57-82). The model has no red ball, and one look serves both groups; next: a red orb with per-frame orb_x/orb_y/orb_r pose keys and per-group look options for f42-f74. egg_y (gargoyle.py) + an egg_y x egg probe now fit the rise (f43 egg_y 40, f44 24, f45 16, f46 8, f48 0), but f42-f46 still fail on IoU 0.834-0.853 (wings/body), so the family stays at 22/73.",
